hiding.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Used the card's menu (Rename/Duplicate/Delete) to Duplicate \\\"Marketing Manager Resume\\\". A new card \\\"Marketing Manager Resume (Copy)\\\" appeared on the dashboard with today's date, containing identical contact/summary/experience/education/skills content. Opened the copy, renamed it to \\\"Marketing Manager Resume V2\\\" via the editor header, and edited its Full Name field to \\\"Sarah Chen EDITED\\\". Returning to the dashboard, the original \\\"Marketing Manager Resume\\\" card remained unchanged (still dated Feb 10, 2024) and reopening it confirmed its Full Name field was untouched (\\\"Sarah Chen\\\", no \\\"EDITED\\\" text present).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Within this session, created a new resume from scratch (\\\"QA Test Resume A\\\", extensively edited with Classic template, 6 experience entries, custom section order/headings), and duplicated an existing resume into an independent copy (\\\"Marketing Manager Resume V2\\\"). The dashboard now lists 5 distinct resumes (QA Test Resume A, Marketing Manager Resume V2, Marketing Manager Resume, Product Designer Resume, Software Engineer Resume), each with independent content, template, and title, demonstrating the app supports creating and managing multiple distinct resume variations concurrently.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dashboard search box filters resumes by title case-insensitively: typing \\\"designer\\\" (lowercase) matched only \\\"Product Designer Resume\\\", and typing \\\"MARKETING\\\" (uppercase) matched both \\\"Marketing Manager Resume V2\\\" and \\\"Marketing Manager Resume\\\". Clearing the search box restored all 5 resumes. Sort combobox offers Newest First/Oldest First/Title A-Z/Title Z-A; selecting \\\"Oldest First\\\" correctly reordered cards ascending by Updated date (Jan 20, 2024 → Feb 10, 2024 → Feb 25, 2024 → Aug 25, 2026 → Aug 25, 2026), confirming both search and sort work as expected.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No date-based filtering feature exists\", \"actual\": \"Inspected the dashboard's full DOM for any filter-by-date control (date input, date-range picker, calendar icon, or \\\"filter\\\" text) - none exists. The only controls present are the title search textbox and the sort-order combobox (Newest First/Oldest First/Title A-Z/Title Z-A). There is no way to filter saved resumes by an exact creation date or date range.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Invalid experience date ranges are not rejected\", \"actual\": \"Setting an experience End Date (2019-01) earlier than its Start Date (2020-01) was accepted with no error, and preview rendered \\\"Jan 2020 - Jan 2019\\\". Setting the End Date to a future date (2027-01) was also accepted with no validation feedback and rendered \\\"Jan 2020 - Jan 2027\\\". No error message, highlighting, or rejection occurred in either case.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Date fields are native month inputs (YYYY-MM) consistently for start/end dates, rendered consistently as \\\"Mon YYYY\\\" in preview (e.g. \\\"Jan 2020\\\"). Checking \\\"I currently work here\\\" cleared and disabled the End Date field (textbox [disabled]) and preview showed \\\"Jan 2020 - Present\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No changes persist across a page reload\", \"actual\": \"After reloading the application (full page navigate to http://localhost:6005/), all session changes were lost: the newly created \\\"QA Test Resume A\\\" and the duplicated \\\"Marketing Manager Resume V2\\\" both disappeared from the dashboard entirely (only the original 3 seed resumes remained), the renamed original resumes reverted to defaults, and \\\"Software Engineer Resume\\\" reverted to its original state - its Updated date reverted to \\\"Jan 20, 2024\\\" (from \\\"Aug 25, 2026\\\"), its phone number reverted to \\\"(555) 123-4567\\\" (losing the edited \\\"(555) 999-0000\\\"), and the added \\\"GraphQL\\\" skill was gone. No created, edited, duplicated, or renamed resumes persisted after reload.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No validation feedback shown for whitespace-only rename\", \"actual\": \"Attempting to rename the resume to a whitespace-only title (\\\"   \\\") was correctly rejected: the title reverted to the previous valid value \\\"QA Test Resume A\\\" and the button/heading displayed it unchanged. However, no error message, toast, or other visible feedback was shown - the Notifications region's list element was confirmed empty (`<ol>...</ol>` with no child nodes) immediately after submission, and no error/invalid/required text appeared anywhere in the page body. The rejection is silent with no user-facing explanation.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Throughout contact/summary/experience/education/skills edits, the Live Preview panel updated immediately after each field change or add/remove/reorder action, with no manual save or refresh needed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Section reorder (move down) and visibility toggle changes were reflected in Live Preview immediately with no manual refresh. Layout change persisted while navigating between tabs during the session (verified order/visibility remained set when switching Template/Sections tabs).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"In \\\"Software Engineer Resume\\\", edited the Phone field and switched to the Skills tab (edit persisted in Live Preview across tab switch), added a new skill \\\"GraphQL\\\", then navigated back to the dashboard. The dashboard card's \\\"Updated\\\" date changed from \\\"Jan 20, 2024\\\" to \\\"Aug 25, 2026\\\" (today), confirming the dashboard reflects the updated status. Reopening the resume confirmed both the new phone number \\\"(555) 999-0000\\\" and the new \\\"GraphQL\\\" skill were retained.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Added 6 experience entries plus summary/education/skills causing preview content height (~2900px) to exceed the visible viewport (~720px). All sections with content (Contact, Employment History with all 6 positions, Career Summary, Academic Background, Core Competencies) rendered fully in the DOM; scrolling (window scrollTo bottom) revealed the last entry \\\"Zeta Ventures / Technical Consultant\\\" confirming no content was clipped and the full resume remains reachable/readable via scrolling.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Same test as IX-14: edited Contact (phone) and Skills (added \\\"GraphQL\\\") content in \\\"Software Engineer Resume\\\", switched between editor tabs, returned to the dashboard, and reopened the resume within the same session. Both the phone number and skill content persisted correctly, confirming section content (contact/skills, and by extension summary/experience/education using the same state mechanism) survives navigation and re-entry during a session.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After duplicating \\\"Marketing Manager Resume\\\" and editing the copy's name field to \\\"Sarah Chen EDITED\\\" plus renaming the copy to \\\"Marketing Manager Resume V2\\\", the original resume's content was verified unaffected (Full Name still \\\"Sarah Chen\\\", title still \\\"Marketing Manager Resume\\\", Updated date unchanged at Feb 10, 2024). Editing the copy did not alter the original, confirming independent content isolation between duplicated resumes.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Renamed resume title to \\\"QA Test Resume A\\\" via the editor header (click-to-edit textbox). The new title is shown correctly as the H1 heading in the editor header, and after navigating back to the dashboard, the same resume's card also displays \\\"QA Test Resume A\\\" as its heading, confirming the rename is reflected both in the editor and on the dashboard card.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Customized Summary section heading not rendered in Minimal template\", \"actual\": \"Renamed the Summary section heading (via Sections tab) to \\\"Career Summary\\\". In Modern and Classic templates, the preview correctly shows an h2 \\\"Career Summary\\\" heading above the summary paragraph. In the Minimal template, no heading is rendered for the Summary section at all (only the paragraph text) - \\\"Career Summary\\\" does not appear anywhere in the DOM. Renamed Work Experience → \\\"Employment History\\\", Education → \\\"Academic Background\\\", and Skills → \\\"Core Competencies\\\" all rendered correctly in all three templates.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
